WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:02.580
What do we do?

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:03.790
What do we do?

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.790
To be able to protect everyone?

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.830
Wait a minute! We're gonna talk it over

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.200
Grownups are so busy

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.330
So busy

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.330
We can't count on them

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.200
That's right

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.080
This town

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.160
We'll help it with Colors Power!

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.660
Pin-pin-pinches come suddenly

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:35.290
And so!

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:35.910
And so?

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:36.500
You know!

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.250
Gear up?

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.700
We have to stay on guard every day

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.120
It looks like our chance

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.250
Which is it?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:44.750
I'm not sure!

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.370
Go on, think

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:45.950
But you know!

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:46.790
Basically

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.290
You don't know until you try

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.830
Peace of mind is far away

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.830
Is what I hear my heart say

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.330
Now be sneaky and bold

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.330
And do your best!

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.450
What times, what times, are the most fun?

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.620
We'll have to investigate more and more

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.950
Do grownups have the energy? They don't have energy

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.080
Kids have energy!

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.700
So leave it all to us!

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.830
We'll do our part with Colors Power!

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.450
Three-Stars Jump!

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.370
It made an emergency landing!

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.450
They don't fly very far.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.870
I'll go next.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:51.580
Because whoever's flies farthest

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:51.580
gets to pick their favorite.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:53.830
Hiya!

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.540
Whoa, that one really flew!

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:00.040
No! I lost!

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.500
I'm next!

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.290
It's all about the wind.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:04.620
Oh, the wind.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.910
No, Koto-chan! Don't give her hints!

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.290
Yah!

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.200
Go! You can do it!

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.080
Fall!

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.830
FALL!

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.540
Why did you take it?!

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:20.910
Yui's last place!

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.120
Stupid Saito-san!

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.410
What do you kids think you're doing?

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.750
Okay, I was first. Let me choose.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.750
I don't know what any of this stuff is.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.700
This could be good!

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.620
It looks cool!

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.950
Nice! I like that one!

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.910
Leave something good for me, too!

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:41.910
Rah!

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.870
Hey. Don't hit anybody with that.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.200
Is there anything else good in here?

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.410
What's this?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.160
A card game?

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.450
That's Menko.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:53.580
Menko?

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.290
You lay the cards out on the ground,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.290
then you throw one down at them.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.370
And whoever flips over the most cards wins.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.290
I think that's how it's played.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.500
Let's try it!

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.250
These cards don't flip over at all!

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.200
Okay, my turn.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.620
Did you get all this from Pops?

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.580
He said it's all the stuff he played with when he was a kid.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.250
It's so retro.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.370
I knew they wouldn't flip over!

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.620
Yeah!

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.500
What's so fun about this, anyway?

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.540
Dangit, kendama!

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.330
This is pretty good.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.620
That's not how kendama works.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.450
Ugh.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.620
Let's pick something else.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:53.830
Yeah.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.330
I like it.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.200
That's not how kendama works.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.410
What's this?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.250
I know that one!

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.330
You have to blow.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.370
Not like that.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.580
You blow into this thing.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.790
I see!

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.790
Here goes!

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.250
Oh, wait, wait!

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:29.160
Let's see here.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.000
Go!

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.160
Oh, are these those supercar erasers?

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.580
It won't fly!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.200
Oh, I think this is...

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.620
You're doing it AGAIN?!

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.790
Come on, let’s stop this already.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:47.540
Well, whatever.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:47.540
Come on, let’s stop this already.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:48.330
Well, whatever.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.700
Oh, no!

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.910
How do you spin a top again?

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.620
What's-so-fun-about-this attack!

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.080
"How to spin a top"...

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.080
One more time!

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.120
I see.

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.040
What's-so-fun-about-this return!

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:11.540
Okay.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.250
Kendama!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.620
I told you that's not how kendama works!

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.450
Here goes!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.330
You busted it.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.790
Sorry. Reflex.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.830
That's okay! We didn't really get it anyway.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:41.000
We don't really get any of this stuff.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.870
Did you find anything fun?

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:46.540
Nope!

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:47.410
Nope!

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.660
I wonder if Pops was trying to tell us

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.660
that he didn't have fun as a kid.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.370
Poor Pops.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.790
I guess we'll have to go play with him sometime!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.410
Is that kendama fun?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.250
Yeah, this one was good.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.370
Koto-chan, let me try!

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.080
Here.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:02.790
Oh, yay!

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.580
Oh. Not bad.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.580
Oh, yay!

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.540
Oh. Not bad.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:15.580
Th-that's just too sad!

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.950
The Poor Elephants

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.580
Did you guys know about this book?

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.080
This elephant story...

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.250
It's just zoo sad!

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:44.870
Huh? Is that a joke?

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.250
And she likes it.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.750
What happens in it?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:57.250
There was a war, so they decided

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:57.250
to kill the elephants by poisoning their food.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:59.870
But they have really long noses,

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:03.540
so they smell really well and knew it was poisoned,

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:03.540
so they didn't eat it.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:07.200
And they died of mal-peanut-rition.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:15.120
Ugh! Stop putting gags in the sad stories!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.540
That didn't make sense.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.950
I'll just read it myself.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.620
It happened during the war.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:30.790
The people were afraid of what would happen 

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:30.790
if the cages at the Ueno Zoo broke open in an air raid.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.160
So they had to kill the animals.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:37.620
Lions, tigers, bears were all given poison and died.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.830
Then it was the elephants' turn.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:45.700
But the clever elephants smelled

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:45.700
the poison in the food and refused to eat it.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.700
The zookeepers had no choice but to

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.700
stop giving them food and water altogether.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.700
The elephants quickly grew thinner and thinner.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.450
Nevertheless, whenever someone passed by their cage,

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:02.830
they would gather up all their strength

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:02.830
to raise their trunks,

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.120
performing the tricks that used to earn them food.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:09.160
Eventually, the elephants starved to death.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:15.660
They died with their trunks stretched out,

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:15.660
still trying to perform their old tricks. 

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:24.870
Poor... poor elephants!

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.290
It's just too sad!

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:28.160
Let me see.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.040
O-okay...

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:37.450
I know!

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.120
Let's go to the zoo right now!

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.200
Yeah! I want to go, too!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.040
You want to go, too, right, Kotoha?

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:51.700
The Poor Elephants

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:48.080
I do.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.160
Are you crying?

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.330
I'm not crying.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.450
Okay! First we'll stop at my house!

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.330
Ameyoko

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:00.000
Kise Fruits

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.410
I'm home!

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:02.790
Hello!

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.750
Oh, welcome back! And hello, girls.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.160
Be back later!

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.580
Goodbye!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:10.790
Uh, o-okay.

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:12.750
See you later!

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:15.580
What were they even doing here?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.830
Ueno Zoo

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.160
Kids through sixth grade get in free?

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:27.910
I knew it would be cheaper because we're kids,

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:27.910
but I didn't expect THIS.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:32.330
When I came here on that field trip,

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:32.330
I didn't realize it was free.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.500
This must mean...

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:38.580
The animals aren't getting any food! I just know it!

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.200
That's terrible!

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:44.830
We are the peacekeepers of this town!

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.040
Colors!

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:50.620
Our mission is to make sure

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:50.620
the animals are alive and well!

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.330
Right!

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.450
Do we really get in free?

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.200
Three children, please!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.120
Yes, go right on in.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.160
Okay, we're on our way, pitiful elephants!

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.200
Piti-phants for short!

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.580
Don't shorten it!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.540
They have pandas!

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:11.950
What?!

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:19.250
It's a panda! A real panda!

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:21.830
A pandy in full view! A full panty!

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:24.040
She thinks it's funny!

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:26.950
And there's a flash panty!

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:28.830
Sat-chan, settle down!

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.160
Huh?

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.540
Hey, that panda is eating.

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:34.870
Yeah.

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:38.370
Come on, don't be such a slacker!

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.580
Get off your grass and start eating that bamboo!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.910
'Cause it's a grass.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:45.700
Was that funny?

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.580
It says symmetry tiger!

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.950
Sumatran Tiger

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.790
It's the same backwards and forwards!

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.040
That's not what it says.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.700
It's so cool.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:06.870
It's a bone!

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.410
See? This is what happens

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.410
when you don't feed the animals.

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:13.370
What? You don't mean that that bone is from a person?

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.870
That bone is pretty big.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.620
If I know one person in this town who's pretty big...

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:21.410
You don't mean...!

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:24.040
Pops!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.660
I have no choice.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:29.700
What?

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:32.040
I will defeat that tiger.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:32.950
What?!

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:36.500
She's right! We are the peacekeepers of this town!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.540
Colors!

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:39.790
We will avenge Pops's death!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.200
What?!

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.500
Sat-chan, you go around. I'll take it from behind.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.660
You got it! Just you wait, Pops!

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.450
We're on our way!

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:50.910
Today, I will defeat a tiger!

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.910
But I think we're already too late.

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:58.080
Wait, Kotoha!

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.410
Take that!

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:02.330
See? That's how it's done!

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:06.040
Um, can I go now?

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:08.450
So you couldn't get in.

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.040
Aww.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.790
Dammit, we couldn't save Pops.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.540
Nocturnal house?

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.000
This looks interesting!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.370
What? No, let's go somewhere else.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:23.250
Let's go in.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:24.200
Going in!

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:29.200
Wait!

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:33.750
Wait for me!

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.540
No! NO!

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:36.750
Something's flying!

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:39.290
They're under me, too!

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.330
You see anything?

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:45.540
No, it was too dark in there.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:49.250
There were things! Lots of things!

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:58.500
Over there!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:12:59.700
Yeah, I see it.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:03.790
Wow.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:06.910
It looked this way!

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:08.250
Come over here!

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:13.000
Monorail Platform

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:18.450
It's free to get in the zoo, but not to use the monorail?

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:23.160
It's about the same as taking the subway.

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:23.160
But there's only one station.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.200
Extortion.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.410
Sorry about that.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:30.120
The zoo doesn't own the monorail.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:34.910
And by the way, this was the first monorail in Japan.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.120
We have to.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.500
If it will help the animals to get even a little more food.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.000
Yeah. It's for the animals.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:45.040
So that Pops will no longer have to be sacrificed.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:48.750
No, I told you, the zoo doesn't make any money from...

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:17.950
Oh. It's a human.

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:20.750
It is! There are humans at this zoo, too?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.660
That's just a normal walkway, right?

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:29.910
Monorail West Park Station

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.410
Penguins!

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.000
Kangaroos!

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.540
Flamingos!

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:45.950
What IS this one?

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:47.370
It's a weird bird.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:48.910
With a weird face.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.250
How to identify a Shoebill

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.370
Showy... bill...

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.330
Shoob... ill?

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.000
Shoe bill?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.500
Hey, look over here!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.080
Hey!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:04.330
Come on, are you free right now?

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.750
Excuse me!

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.580
It won't react!

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:09.870
Woh-pah!

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:11.160
Huh?

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.250
Hyaa!

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.700
HYAAAH!

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:24.620
It's not working.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:25.870
Nope.

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.200
Not working.

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.660
Oh, look! What's that?

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.200
Right this way for your guided tour!

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.040
Guided tour?

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:40.200
Animal Eating

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:40.200
Habits

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:40.000
Today our theme is animal eating habits.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:43.080
You know there was a tiger eating a guy over there.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.000
What?!

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.660
Oh, you mean that bone?

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:49.870
Guided Tour

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:49.870
Meeting

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:49.870
Point

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:49.910
Don't worry. That was a cow bone.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.410
It's eating a cow, and you're telling us NOT to worry?!

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:54.040
Huh?

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.080
Mm-hm, yeah!

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:57.290
That didn't make it better?

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:59.290
Well cows are animals, too!

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.000
I thought this was a zoo!

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.160
Mm-hm, yeah!

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.000
Uh, well...

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:06.870
Well what about pandas?

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:11.080
All they eat is bamboo,

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:11.080
but it costs more than ten thousand yen a day.

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:12.370
Isn't that amazing?

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.040
Ten thousand yen?

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:18.040
Incidentally, my daily eating expenses

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:18.040
are five hundred yen.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.410
Are the pandas making you poor?

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:22.790
No, I wouldn't say...

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:25.750
We have to check on all the other animals!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.040
You're right, Leader! Let's go!

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.120
Yeah!

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.120
What? Don't you want a tour?

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:30.790
What? Don't you want a tour?

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:44.120
It's a sheep!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:45.120
It's a goat.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:46.790
It's a Genghis Khan!

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:49.000
How do you know the difference?

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:50.160
Flavor.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:52.580
It stinks! It's a Genghis Khan!

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:55.950
Come now and you can hold a house mouse!

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.080
Would anyone like to try it?

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.000
What?

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.290
We can hold them?

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.580
It's so little! So cute!

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:15.620
House mice are fully grown

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:15.620
and can have babies at two months old.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.700
They multiply very quickly.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.830
I thought so.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.830
Huh? What is it, Kotoha?

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:26.450
They multiply quickly, but there are only a few here.

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:31.120
I bet they're using these house mice

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:31.120
as food for the other animals.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.330
What?!

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:35.250
That's how they can afford to let people in for free!

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.000
Is that true?

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:37.500
Free, huh?

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.660
Excuse me, everyone. We don't do that.

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.660
Free, huh?

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.620
Excuse me, everyone. We don't do that.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.870
He looks a little like Saito.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:52.750
That's the face of a liar.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:53.700
Yeah.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:54.830
You may be right.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:56.330
What?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:07.080
Look over here.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.200
Is that Pops?

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:12.540
Note: A character in a folktale who rescues a turtle

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:12.540
that then in turn takes him to an ocean palace.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.250
I'm gonna be Urashima!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.330
It looks good, Kotoha!

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:19.870
It's so tall!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:24.830
Oh! Did it just poop?

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.830
Jeez, you don't have to say that, Sat-chan.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.250
Come to think of it,

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.250
that's the first time I said poop all day!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.330
You're right! That's unusual.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:40.040
The zoo sure is a lot of fun!

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:40.750
Yeah!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.580
Next time, I'll beat that tiger.

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:46.040
The tiger and all the other animals

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:46.040
were getting enough to eat.

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.910
Yup! And they were pooping, too!

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.160
But that ain't the point!

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.660
What's wrong, Sat-chan?

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.330
It's not relephant...

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.000
It's elephant!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:56.660
Huh?

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:57.830
The elephants!

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.950
We haven't seen the elephants!

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.330
Oh yeah, elephants! I forgot!

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.410
As we stand here talking...

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:09.160
the piti-phants might be starving to death!

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:13.410
Says the girl who raced off to see the pandas.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:17.200
Let's see, the elephants are...

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:19.410
By the entrance!

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.160
Elephants!

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:27.250
We're stampeding your way!

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:28.830
We're coming, elephants! 

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:30.450
Just you weight!

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:32.330
We're coming!

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:34.370
Keep your trunks on!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:39.330
Elephants...

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.410
Sat-chan!

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:45.120
I finally found you!

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:47.700
My piti-phants!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.750
They look healthy!

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:00.950
What a relief. They're getting enough to eat.

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:04.200
Yeah!

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.410
But their skin's so dry and leathery.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.000
They should see the pachy-dermatologist.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.700
Am I right?

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:11.910
Huh?

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.540
They're huge. They must be strong.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:19.950
But I guess that's a wasted apple.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:19.950
I brought it in case they weren't doing so good.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.870
Is that why we stopped by your house?

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:25.830
But you shouldn't feed them without permission.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.830
I know that! There's only one thing to do.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:31.080
Food coming your way!

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.540
Announcing it doesn't make it better!

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.040
It ate it!

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:47.000
That's so cool!

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.410
In one bite!

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:51.250
Did you like my family's apple?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:55.540
I'll bring more, so wait with your nose outstretched!

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:56.910
'Cause you're an elephant!

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.330
That's ARMS outstretched!

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:03.330
It's waving its trunk!

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:05.120
It's a happy-derm.

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:06.580
Am I right?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:07.370
Huh?

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:11.000
Caution

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:11.000
Please do not feed the animals.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.540
Our sparkling signal is the first star

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.580
Oops, time to go home

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:27.620
Later, Colors!

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.700
Later, Colors!

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:31.790
The peace is kept another day

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:32.540
We did it!

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.790
Total victory for us!

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:38.950
A chu-chu-cabrilla out on a walk

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.910
Take that! Extra virgin oil!

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:44.750
We're really busy every day

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:47.080
Cases from level one to how high?

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.080
We'll solve any mystery!

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:50.200
I've beat this game!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:51.120
There it is!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.080
Call us again when you're in a pinch!

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:56.290
For the peace of this town!

00:21:56.450 --> 00:22:00.950
Saying, "Ready, go!" with the orange sky

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:04.870
Let's go home together

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:09.080
Tomorrow we can probably have even more excitement

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:11.910
We all dash to meet at the hideout

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:17.160
Goodbye, sun. Goodnight, town

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:21.250
I can't wait for tomorrow

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:25.290
My heart won't stop skipping in excitement

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:29.620
Another day and all's well!

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:32.200
See you tomorrow!

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:33.750
One more time!

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:38.120
See you tomorrow!

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:46.500
Well, we took a break last week, but this week, 

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:46.500
we're having our Colors Evaluation Meeting!

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:48.370
We'll start with you, Kotoha!

00:22:48.370 --> 00:22:50.870
You know what my biggest regret for today was.

00:22:51.040 --> 00:22:53.790
I couldn't save Pops from the tiger at the zoo.

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:55.660
Now he's just bones!

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:59.330
Huh? But on the way home,

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:59.330
we saw him in front of his shop, didn't we?

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:04.830
I believe that when he gave me the kendama earlier,

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:04.830
he wanted me to use it to save him.

00:23:04.830 --> 00:23:06.700
It was an SOS.

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:08.620
Oh, is THAT what it was?!

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:10.870
But we saw Pops, didn't we?

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:13.580
What a shame. We lost our dear, dear Pops.

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:16.290
Maybe I was the only one who saw him.

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:18.910
Don't tell me that was Pops's ghost?!

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:21.540
Um, Sat-chan, what do you have to say?

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:24.450
I got to feed the piti-phants, so it was a good day!

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:27.120
But you're not really supposed to feed them.

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:31.620
And I got to see a lot of animals poop,

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:31.620
so it was a good day!

00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:33.160
Poop again...

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:35.080
Don't you have anything to say, Yui?

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.580
Um, well, I...

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:41.040
I was really happy to get to go to the zoo with-
